  "review_questions": [
    "Did the review identify the defect at pi-extension/src/host/read-only-session.ts:201 and pi-extension/dist/host/read-only-session.js:171 (the expression `if (reason) trustLoadedSession(reader);`): The reload guard in trustStartedSession is inverted to a truthiness test: `reason !== \"reload\"` becomes `reason`. A reload (reason \"reload\", which is truthy) now sets a trust point although Pi did not re-read the file. After a failed write, memory can hold an entry the file lacks and routing would treat it as persisted. The commit's rule is that a reload establishes no trust point. The dist file is mirrored so the committed tests, which import dist, exercise the seed. Did it support the finding with the file and line?",
